swer/id #uuid "c27e5971-1095-5a43-911e-f307b4661072" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296295} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd56023b-3229-5303-9a27-d7d899372fb2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297058}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6cdd99a5-da9f-5683-9b18-848bbade62d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-316652" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=3,{x}_{2,3}=1\\pm 2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $6.$ Find $f(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,-$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2,3}=1\\pm 2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=6,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =6(x-3)(x-(1+2\\text{i}))(x-(1-2\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(x-3)(x-(1+2\\text{i}))(x-(1-2\\text{i})) &= 6(x-3)({x}^{2}-x(1+2\\text{i})-x(1-2\\text{i})+(1+2\\text{i})(1-2\\text{i})) \\\\ &= 6(x-3)({x}^{2}-2x+5) \\\\ &= 6({x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+11x-15) \\\\ &= 6{x}^{3}-30{x}^{2}+66x-90.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=6{x}^{3}-30{x}^{2}+66x-90.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297530 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "062f9756-adec-53a7-8379-fb26972cfb4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "062f9756-adec-53a7-8379-fb26972cfb4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295296} :answer-field/id #uuid "77cda0