e/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "10231f19-13c6-5529-abc7-f00f49668d0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-316656" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=5,{x}_{2,3}=-1\\pm 2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-4.$ Find $f(x).$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=5$ and ${x}_{2,3}=-1\\pm 2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =-4(x-5)(x-(-1+2\\text{i}))(x-(-1-2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =-4(x-5)(x-(-1+2\\text{i}))(x-(-1-2\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4(x-5)(x-(-1+2\\text{i}))(x-(-1-2\\text{i})) &= -4(x-5)({x}^{2}-x(-1-2\\text{i})-x(-1+2\\text{i})+(-1+2\\text{i})(-1-2\\text{i})) \\\\ &= -4(x-5)({x}^{2}+2x+5) \\\\ &= -4({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+5x-5{x}^{2}-10x-25) \\\\ &= -4({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-5x-25) \\\\ &= -4{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}+20x+100.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=-4{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}+20x+100.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297531 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f56c0188-9ee5-539b-9b82-92e1761a2835" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f56c0188-9ee5-539b-9b82-92e1761a2835" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296567} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ffdd945-54a8-5932-b1bc-495e87726382" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296789} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "