9" :question/problem "![](images/b2/b2dbc407d70f4e6d3cf35dd24e1a6fb7d463207631a0498595ed40550ac86433.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a cubic polynomial $f(x).$\nFind $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $-5.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 2\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-5.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =-5(x-3)(x-2\\text{i})(x-(-2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =-5(x-3)(x-2\\text{i})(x+2\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5(x-3)(x-2\\text{i})(x+2\\text{i}) &= -5(x-3)({x}^{2}+x(2\\text{i})-x(2\\text{i})-(2\\text{i})^{2}) \\\\ &= -5(x-3)({x}^{2}+4) \\\\ &= -5({x}^{3}+4x-3{x}^{2}-12) \\\\ &= -5{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}-20x+60.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=-5{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}-20x+60.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297534 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63e03f80-4dd0-5d82-a864-30b1e2ea28a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63e03f80-4dd0-5d82-a864-30b1e2ea28a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295836} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e5d85b4-3799-5a6d-b7b0-23336806a7d9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296720} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bcdb2d84-aca1-5931-a861-326e29795bc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296261}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bcdb2d84-aca1-5931-a861-326e29795bc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296261} :answer-field/id #uuid "518a35c0-0e1c-5d28-a563-8edb4f1f2c50" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296794} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0e6e712-1816-5633-a72c-c3521f30498a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0e6e712-1816-5633-a72c-c3521f30498a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296364} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e5c7ed3-3d5d-57d9-9b64-7ab92874c7e1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296829} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a644278-b479-57d0-a381-e958365236f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295936}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a644278-b479-57d0-a381-e958365236f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295936} :answer-field/id #uuid "9de18d62-3991-55f0-8128-db43d1496140" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296964}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dd1fb75a-89ec-5672-ba77-4f8556ccd77f" :question/math-academy-id "q-316704" :question/problem "![](images/ce/ce15895aa3a0f7e7cbea820e06a3c56aadef1d440b59120db17c5df394970adb.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a cubic polynomial $f(x).$\nFind $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $-7.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=1$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 4\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-7.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =-7(x-1)(x-4\\text{i})(x-(-4\\text{i})) \\\\  & =-7(x-1)(x-4\\text{i})(x+4\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7(x-1)(x-4\\text{i})(x+4\\text{i}) &= -7(x-1)({x}^{2}+x(4\\text{i})-x(4\\text{i})-(4\\text{i})^{2}) \\\\ &= -7(x-1)({x}^{2}+16) \\\\ &= -7({x}^{3}+16x-{x}^{2}-16) \\\\ &= -7{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-112x+112.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=-7{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-112x+112.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297535 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee8d7975-444e-580c-8143-058f8ed48a56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee8d7975-444e-580c-8143-058f8ed48a56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296534} :answer-field/id #uuid "5dc2b55b-8207-59a2-adc4-4d98c2f428f2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296826} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5735bff5-2b04-5fd6-98d5-f1fef777b973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5735bff5-2b04-5fd6-98d5-f1fef777b973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295772} :answer-field/id #uuid "793a3da5-347c-5d89-8511-55fdf7ba1ccf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296882} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6c9c4ff-48a5-5b4f-8ec3-7a7ffd64a0df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6c9c4ff-48a5-5b4f-8ec3-7a7ffd64a0df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296494} :answer-field/id #uuid "93772ffa-573f-5fd7-8ec9-cef9dafb7da0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296937} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d980f004-e962-5f3a-838a-fb999f3a260d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "216" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d980f004-e962-5f3a-838a-fb999f3a260d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "216" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296417} :answer-field/id #uuid "96b8f953-f686-514d-8435-0f036ad21ad7" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296950}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b503e515-255f-56bc-8cff-21d5e4bbae13" :question/math-academy-id "q-316707" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=6,\\,{x}_{2,3}=\\pm 3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-4.$ Find $f(x).$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=6$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =-4(x-6)(x-3\\text{i})(x-(-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =-4(x-6)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4(x-6)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i}) &= -4(x-6)({x}^{2}-x(-3\\text{i})-x(3\\text{i})+(3\\text{i})(-3\\text{i})) \\\\ &= -4(x-6)({x}^{2}+9) \\\\ &= -4({x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+9x-54) \\\\ &= -4{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-36x+216.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=-4{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-36x+216.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297538 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9752c91-162b-546d-abb1-86090fbf82a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296416}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9752c91-162b-546d-abb1-86090fbf82a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296416} :answer-field/id #uuid "3baa4431-f8c9-5e9e-bbc1-101ff5c75a54" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296749} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "756b2b89-32ac-5b19-b401-05cbd62d448d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "756b2b89-32ac-5b19-b401-05cbd62d448d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295907} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c070d44-8a4d-52e3-a156-4ce0e99f7240" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296750} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5dd426f-e4e0-5f4d-9d8a-2c8c2f108ab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296572}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5dd426f-e4e0-5f4d-9d8a-2c8c2f108ab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296572} :answer-field/id #uuid "f74a3812-6626-5faa-88c2-727dea6b273d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297141}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d76039a2-01f1-5d8a-a55a-8960fd4792dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-316725" :question/problem "![](images/dd/dd92f4b41c95c436027cce015b688df1a982f46913b0ea262f2d30e1e49259d5.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $-2.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2,3}=-1\\pm 3\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-2.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =-2(x-2)(x-(-1+3\\text{i}))(x-(-1-3\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(x-2)(x-(-1+3\\text{i}))(x-(-1-3\\text{i})) &= -2(x-2)({x}^{2}-x(-1-3\\text{i})-x(-1+3\\text{i})+(-1+3\\text{i})(-1-3\\text{i})) \\\\ &= -2(x-2)({x}^{2}+2x+10) \\\\ &= -2({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+10x-2{x}^{2}-4x-20) \\\\ &= -2({x}^{3}+6x-20) \\\\ &= -2{x}^{3}-12x+40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=-2{x}^{3}-12x+40.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299818 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abf3f8cf-9118-5e4d-9983-aee3340ebd42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}+21{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abf3f8cf-9118-5e4d-9983-aee3340ebd42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}+21{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298300} :answer-field/id #uuid "9cf634a6-7cdf-5acc-9a45-0ea71ed3813a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299153}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "319cb10c-24a8-524b-9096-0eba7af16ccf" :question/math-academy-id "q-320074" :question/problem "![](images/fb/fb8d76e5fb2e83676fbab4178b523bf8cbff076490f12fa8be17c37ce06e1820.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Determine the **expanded form** of $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $1.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,100$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1,2}=\\pm 2,$ and ${x}_{3,4}=\\pm 5\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=1.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =1(x-2)(x-(-2))(x-5\\text{i})(x-(-5\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(x-2)(x+2)(x-5\\text{i})(x+5\\text{i}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)(x+2)(x-5\\text{i})(x+5\\text{i}) &= ({x}^{2}+2x-2x-4)({x}^{2}+5\\text{i}x-5\\text{i}x-(5\\text{i})^{2}) \\\\ &= ({x}^{2}-4)({x}^{2}+25) \\\\ &= {x}^{4}+25{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2}-100 \\\\ &= {x}^{4}+21{x}^{2}-100.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)={x}^{4}+21{x}^{2}-100.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299829 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7595fe8f-ad2e-54d9-9fae-ed9ba3ad07ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{4}+74{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7595fe8f-ad2e-54d9-9fae-ed9ba3ad07ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{4}+74{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298062} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0bddcc8-d368-5c66-aa8a-891ed665fb3e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299236}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d2d05cab-afc8-555d-96ed-d65f47562369" :question/math-academy-id "q-320185" :question/problem "![](images/6a/6a39af16798593716291ab84bfff4460279420f493bd10959782312187f0bf44.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Determine the **expanded form** of $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $2.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,72$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1,2}=\\pm \\text{i}$ and ${x}_{3,4}=\\pm 6\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=2.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =2(x-(-\\text{i}))(x-\\text{i})(x-(-6\\text{i}))(x-6\\text{i}) \\\\  & =2(x+\\text{i})(x-\\text{i})(x+6\\text{i})(x-6\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+\\text{i})(x-\\text{i})(x+6\\text{i})(x-6\\text{i}) &= 2({x}^{2}+(\\text{i}-\\text{i})x-{\\text{i}}^{2})({x}^{2}+(6\\text{i}-6\\text{i})x-36{\\text{i}}^{2}) \\\\ &= 2({x}^{2}+1)({x}^{2}+36) \\\\ &= 2({x}^{4}+36{x}^{2}+{x}^{2}+36) \\\\ &= 2({x}^{4}+37{x}^{2}+36) \\\\ &= 2{x}^{4}+74{x}^{2}+72.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=2{x}^{4}+74{x}^{2}+72.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299830 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f999c5b4-de32-59fc-b481-6260fadc576e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}+14{x}^{2}-36x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f999c5b4-de32-59fc-b481-6260fadc576e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}+14{x}^{2}-36x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298614} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb6820c4-e21a-5c85-a33f-afe0d668e46e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299318}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "40827e6d-ccf8-5737-bd80-bc43201366b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-320235" :question/problem "![](images/4f/4f960f00fbcbde79dee3603112ed08e8c34cf87b3ccbe781ee5acbf61a4482fd.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Determine the **expanded form** of $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $2.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,52$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1,2}=-2\\pm 3\\text{i},$ and ${x}_{3,4}=1\\pm \\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=2.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =2(x-(-2+3\\text{i}))(x-(-2-3\\text{i}))(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-(-2+3\\text{i}))(x-(-2-3\\text{i}))(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i})) &= 2({x}^{2}+4x+4+9)({x}^{2}-2x+1+1) \\\\ &= 2({x}^{2}+4x+13)({x}^{2}-2x+2) \\\\ &= 2({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+4{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+8x+13{x}^{2}-26x+26) \\\\ &= 2({x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-18x+26) \\\\ &= 2{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}+14{x}^{2}-36x+52.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=2{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}+14{x}^{2}-36x+52.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299832 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff83a703-e2b6-5e9b-b1f1-a8e5886909df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{4}+9{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-30x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff83a703-e2b6-5e9b-b1f1-a8e5886909df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{4}+9{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-30x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298645} :answer-field/id #uuid "a070ab62-6304-5c58-8645-5a11ed7e0868" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299168}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7837fbb5-9b5f-5218-b805-da7b7a49139e" :question/math-academy-id "q-320276" :question/problem "![](images/58/58136b4140d772431a823b66b03ebfa95bd51816e4df9be7f2401c29c97a5495.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Determine the **expanded form** of $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $3.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,36$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-3,$ ${x}_{2}=2,$ and ${x}_{3,4}=-1\\pm \\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=3.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =3(x-(-3))(x-2)(x-(-1+\\text{i}))(x-(-1-\\text{i})) \\\\  & =3(x+3)(x-2)(x-(-1+\\text{i}))(x-(-1-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+3)(x-2)(x-(-1+\\text{i}))(x-(-1-\\text{i})) &= 3({x}^{2}-2x+3x-6)({x}^{2}-x(-1-\\text{i})-x(-1+\\text{i})+(-1+\\text{i})(-1-\\text{i})) \\\\ &= 3({x}^{2}+x-6)\\,({x}^{2}+2x+2) \\\\ &= 3({x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+2x-6{x}^{2}-12x-12) \\\\ &= 3({x}^{4}+3{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-10x-12) \\\\ &= 3{x}^{4}+9{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-30x-36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=3{x}^{4}+9{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-30x-36.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299835 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45e59df5-3b75-5d09-8a03-b2c44c10e10f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+18{x}^{2}-24x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45e59df5-3b75-5d09-8a03-b2c44c10e10f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+18{x}^{2}-24x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297839} :answer-field/id #uuid "286eceb7-c4c0-59a8-bec4-1493ea987840" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298772}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "25d4cc1b-6157-5691-8648-fe2233c0942f" :question/math-academy-id "q-320292" :question/problem "![](images/4e/4eafeae1c77e3e75cb2b281181346eeb7e96ca5e1bd15ec11d722109469557a1.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Determine the **expanded form** of $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $3.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,24$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1,2}=\\pm 2\\text{i}$  and ${x}_{3,4}=1\\pm \\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=3.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =3(x-2\\text{i})(x-(-2\\text{i}))(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i})) \\\\  & =3(x-2\\text{i})(x+2\\text{i})(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x-2\\text{i})(x+2\\text{i})(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i})) &= 3({x}^{2}+2\\text{i}x-2\\text{i}x-(2\\text{i})^{2})({x}^{2}-x(1-\\text{i})-x(1+\\text{i})+(1+\\text{i})(1-\\text{i})) \\\\ &= 3({x}^{2}+4)({x}^{2}-2x+2) \\\\ &= 3({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+4{x}^{2}-8x+8) \\\\ &= 3({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-8x+8) \\\\ &= 3{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+18{x}^{2}-24x+24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=3{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+18{x}^{2}-24x+24\\,.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314985 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "027eecbf-7d9e-56b4-a605-18bbb53e14b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311977} {:answer/id #uuid "4494fa18-4bec-52af-830e-3d47e3335b32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312528} {:answer/id #uuid "9649e93c-dcb4-5673-af2c-491163f8d92d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313174} {:answer/id #uuid "d90019b4-a024-5ea2-b7e9-d632c152b387" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313682} {:answer/id #uuid "e664ec95-b5dd-5b08-ac1e-628c8f111a90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9649e93c-dcb4-5673-af2c-491163f8d92d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313174} :answer-field/id #uuid "271f0e63-bff4-53c7-a28b-a628905d21bb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314113} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "084986f6-01c0-508d-b7b2-e49ecf7afbf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{2}+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312035} {:answer/id #uuid "1b9be0ef-0626-58f6-8f34-f07d2341cc36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{2}+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312179} {:answer/id #uuid "1ee209f2-de18-556a-b781-2693cbbb09b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({x}^{2}+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312209} {:answer/id #uuid "4c486615-805d-5bc0-8681-1ee3c3e17ff9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{2}+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312592} {:answer/id #uuid "9a09cad1-8a04-5089-8601-85ab90a53a71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{2}+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313194} {:answer/id #uuid "e661e1e8-358c-5402-8b71-9182bd7c2769" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({x}^{2}+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "084986f6-01c0-508d-b7b2-e49ecf7afbf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{2}+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312035} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dd294ec-abdf-52bd-adbb-82925e22c66c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314178} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2adde187-25b8-5d4b-a204-1561619be2dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312303} {:answer/id #uuid "44b54432-6be2-557b-86a3-52063866fc0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312530} {:answer/id #uuid "91d08667-08e2-52ae-8373-62b7feb36f57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313142} {:answer/id #uuid "b45c048e-2b73-557d-9a93-c538814c0f85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313379} {:answer/id #uuid "c2c63573-93e1-5481-abea-0476f7532355" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44b54432-6be2-557b-86a3-52063866fc0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312530} :answer-field/id #uuid "48c5f513-5509-5ed5-bf44-fe4e4be503ff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314217}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "189f6686-0cc6-5c02-8e21-1097f02fd5af" :question/math-academy-id "q-340628" :question/problem "Let $F(x)={x}^{2}+3$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${a}_{3}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that is piecewise continuous over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ &= ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ \\\\ &= ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ \\\\ &= \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n{a}_{3}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi -(-\\pi ))+\\frac{1}{12}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-6\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & ={a}_{3}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ \\\\ {a}_{3} & =\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{2}+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314987 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08fed8a6-dde9-59a6-bc31-184c4876910c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312040} {:answer/id #uuid "27e0630f-6397-5f50-acaf-792c1ed4a63f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312279} {:answer/id #uuid "43aed6aa-dcf1-5ad7-a81d-0980770c21f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\